---
import MainLayout from '@/layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import LegalFooter from '@/components/LegalFooter.astro';
import { PAGE_DESCRIPTIONS } from '@/lib/seo/defaults';
import '@/styles/legal-pages.css';
---

<MainLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Kersivo"
  description={PAGE_DESCRIPTIONS.terms}
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <article class="container legal-page__inner">
      <h1 class="legal-page__title">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="legal-page__updated">Last updated: 14 July 2026</p>

      <p>
        These Terms govern the provision of barbershop website, booking, and retail pickup software and related services
        offered under the Kersivo name. They are intended for business customers (barbershops) in the UK. They do not
        constitute legal advice; have them reviewed for your situation.
      </p>

      <h2>Parties</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>Service provider</strong> is <strong>Bartosz Jasinski</strong>, operating as a freelancer in
        Bournemouth, United Kingdom. References to &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo; and &ldquo;our&rdquo; mean the
        Service provider. For enquiries, contact
        <a href="mailto:hello@kersivo.co.uk">hello@kersivo.co.uk</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Client</strong> means the barbershop or business that orders the work. By using the service after we
        confirm your order or give you access, you agree to these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>What we provide</h2>
      <p>Depending on your subscription, services may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>a bespoke or brief-led marketing website;</li>
        <li>integrated online booking on your domain;</li>
        <li>an admin panel for team, diary, retail, and reports;</li>
        <li>buy-and-collect retail with checkout through Stripe on <strong>your</strong> Stripe account;</li>
        <li>ongoing hosting and support while your subscription is active.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Feature lists and fees on our <a href="/#pricing">pricing page</a> form part of these Terms by reference.
        KERSIVO takes <strong>0% KERSIVO commission</strong> on bookings and retail sales.
        <strong>Standard Stripe payment-processing fees still apply</strong> under your agreement with Stripe.
      </p>

      <h2>Admin access</h2>
      <p>
        When you sign in to the barbershop admin panel, we use necessary first-party session cookies so you can stay
        signed in for your convenience and security (typically for up to 30 days). Details are set out in our
        <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a> and <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Fees and payment</h2>
      <p>
        Fees are as shown on our pricing page: <strong>£39/month subscription</strong>. There is
        <strong> no setup fee</strong>. Billing starts when you subscribe and renews monthly via Stripe unless we agree
        otherwise in writing.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Prices shown are final. KERSIVO is not currently VAT registered, so no VAT is added.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2 id="subscription">Monthly subscription</h2>
      <p>
        The KERSIVO monthly subscription is <strong>£39/month</strong>, billed automatically, unless we agree a
        different rate in writing. There is <strong>no minimum term</strong> and <strong>no notice period</strong>.
        You may cancel at any time; the service remains active until the end of the paid month.
      </p>
      <p>While your subscription is active, it includes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>custom site, booking, admin and pickup shop setup;</li>
        <li>hosting;</li>
        <li>SSL;</li>
        <li>platform and security updates;</li>
        <li>maintenance;</li>
        <li>support;</li>
        <li>domain purchase, management and renewal;</li>
        <li>transactional emails;</li>
        <li>booking, admin and retail systems;</li>
        <li>up to one hour of minor development changes per month;</li>
        <li>email appointment confirmations and reminders.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Automated SMS appointment reminders are <strong>not yet enabled</strong> as a standard platform feature.
        If SMS is required for your launch, agree it with us in writing at setup.
      </p>

      <h2>If your subscription ends</h2>
      <p>
        After the end of the paid month following cancellation, the
        <strong>website, booking system, admin dashboard and retail system are taken offline</strong>. There is no
        self-serve way to keep those systems running without an active subscription.
      </p>

      <h2>Domain name</h2>
      <p>
        You are the <strong>registrant and owner</strong> of your domain name. While your subscription is active, KERSIVO
        purchases, manages and renews the domain on your behalf. After cancellation, we transfer management control to
        you. The KERSIVO platform is <strong>not</strong> transferred with the domain.
      </p>

      <h2>Stripe and retail</h2>
      <p>
        Online card payments for live shops use <strong>Stripe</strong> on <strong>your Stripe account</strong>
        (you remain the seller of record). The public <strong>/shop</strong> retail demo is a
        <strong>simulation only</strong>: no payment is taken, no Stripe Checkout session is created, and no order is
        stored. Private owner shop tests in the admin may create <strong>marked test orders</strong> without payment so
        you can practise the pickup workflow. Before go-live, retail and deposit checkout for your live shop is connected
        to <strong>your Stripe account</strong> as part of setup delivery. You are responsible for complying with
        Stripe&rsquo;s terms, for accurate pricing and product descriptions, and for your own tax and legal obligations as
        seller. Pickup-only fulfilment and returns policies are set and operated by you unless we agree otherwise in
        writing. Standard Stripe payment-processing fees still apply under the Stripe account that receives the funds.
      </p>

      <h2>Data ownership, export, and leaving</h2>
      <p>
        You own your domain, brand, content, client relationship and exported business data. KERSIVO does not sell your
        client data.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may request a <strong>free CSV export</strong> containing first name, surname where stored, email, phone
        number and booking history. Export is available while your subscription is active and for
        <strong>30 days after termination</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is <strong>no lock-in</strong>: you may cancel your subscription at any time (service continues to the end of
        the paid month). How we handle personal data (including your clients&rsquo; data) is described in our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your content and intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        You retain ownership of your branding, text, images, and other materials you supply. You grant us a licence to
        host, display, and use them solely to deliver the project and run the service for you.
      </p>
      <p>
        KERSIVO owns the source code, platform, admin software, retail software and infrastructure. Your subscription to
        Your subscription gives you a <strong>licence</strong> to use the platform while it is active; it does
        <strong>not</strong> transfer ownership of the underlying software to you.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        You will not use the service for unlawful activity, to infringe others&rsquo; rights, or to transmit malware. You
        are responsible for the accuracy of opening hours, services, and product information shown to the public.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability and support</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to keep the service reasonably available but do not guarantee uninterrupted access. Support response
        times for subscribed clients are within one business day as described on our website.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, loss of
        profit, or loss of data, except where such exclusion is not allowed by law. Our total liability arising out of
        or relating to these Terms in any twelve-month period is limited to the fees you paid us for the service in that
        period, except for death, personal injury caused by negligence, fraud, or other liability that cannot be limited
        by law. Nothing in these Terms is intended to exclude or restrict any rights you may have under applicable UK law.
      </p>

      <h2>Force majeure</h2>
      <p>
        We are not liable for delay or failure caused by events outside our reasonable control (for example outages of
        major cloud providers, strikes, or natural disasters).
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the law of England and Wales. Any dispute arising out of or in connection with
        these Terms that cannot be resolved by negotiation will be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the
        courts of England and Wales.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms. We will post the new version on this page and change the &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo;
        date. For active clients, material changes may also be communicated by email or through the admin where
        appropriate.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <LegalFooter />
</MainLayout>
